1
00:08:16,666 --> 00:08:22,666
The End is a drama, music film directed by Joshua Oppenheimer.

2
00:16:33,333 --> 00:16:39,333
Twenty-five years after environmental collapse left the Earth uninhabitable, Mother, Father and Son are confined to their palatial bunker, where they struggle to
maintain hope and a sense of normalcy by clinging to the rituals of daily life—until the arrival of a stranger, Girl, upends their happy routine.

3
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:56,000
As tensions rise, their seemingly idyllic existence starts to crumble.

4
00:33:06,666 --> 00:33:12,666
Mother, played by Tilda Swinton.

5
00:41:23,333 --> 00:41:29,333
Son, played by George MacKay.

6
00:49:40,000 --> 00:49:46,000
Girl, played by Moses Ingram.

7
00:57:56,666 --> 00:58:02,666
Father, played by Michael Shannon.

8
01:06:13,333 --> 01:06:19,333
Friend, played by Bronagh Gallagher.

9
01:14:30,000 --> 01:14:36,000
Butler, played by Tim McInnerny.

10
01:22:46,666 --> 01:22:52,666
The End is a 2024 apocalyptic musical film directed
and co-written by Joshua Oppenheimer.

11
01:31:03,333 --> 01:31:09,333
Produced by Oppenheimer, Signe Byrge Sørensen, and star Tilda Swinton, the film also features George
MacKay, Moses Ingram, Bronagh Gallagher, Tim McInnerny, Lennie James, and Michael Shannon.

12
01:39:20,000 --> 01:39:26,000
The story follows a wealthy family living in an underground bunker, after a global environmental
disaster leaves Earth inhospitable, whose dynamics alter following the arrival of a survivor.

13
01:47:36,666 --> 01:47:42,666
The End premiered at the 51st Telluride Film Festival on 31 August 2024.

14
01:55:53,333 --> 01:55:59,333
It was released by Neon in the United States on 6 December 2024.

15
02:04:10,000 --> 02:04:16,000
The film received a mixed reception from critics.

16
02:12:26,666 --> 02:12:32,666
The film explores themes of bunker, post-apocalyptic future, musical.

17
02:20:43,333 --> 02:20:49,333
The tone is emotional.
